* `radixPass k`, `radixSort kb`: the pure stable partition pass / LSD radix sort on the first
  component (the key) of each record; `radixSort_keys`: for keys forming a permutation of
  `0, …, N-1` (with `N ≤ 2^kb`) the record with key `q` ends up at position `q`.
* `passP w`, `sortP w`: the register programs (records of width `w ≥ 1` on stack `0`, record
  count on `1`, key bits `kb` on `2`; scratch `46 … 53`); `sortP_spec`, `sortP_cost`.
